#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/installation-and-upgrade/partials/snippet-certificate-validators.adoc:2
msgid "If your installation uses an older self-signed CA generated by {productname}, you might need to create a new CA and new server certificates, then deploy the new root CA to all clients."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/installation-and-upgrade/partials/snippet-certificate-validators.adoc:3
msgid "You can rotate the CA certificate on a Podman installation using the new `mgradm ssl` command.  For more information, see xref:administration:ssl-certs-ca-migration.adoc[]."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/installation-and-upgrade/partials/snippet-certificate-validators.adoc:4
msgid "Note that the command can only be used *after* upgrading both `mgradm` and {productname}.  You can safely upgrade affected installations as long as you rotate the CA certificates and ensure clients recognize them before starting the server."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/installation-and-upgrade/partials/snippet-certificate-validators.adoc:5
msgid "While failing to rotate the CA certificate may not cause an immediate system failure, it is strongly discouraged."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/installation-and-upgrade/partials/snippet-check-rpmnew-rpmsave.adoc:1
msgid "In some upgrades, multiple `+*.rpmnew+` and `+*.rpmsave+` files may be generated. The presence or number of these files does not indicate that manual action is required. In SUSE Multi-Linux Manager container environments, required configuration changes are applied automatically during the upgrade process. These files are created as a result of differences between packaged defaults and existing configuration files, and may also include internal or informational changes that are not intended to be merged. If manual action is required for a configuration change, it will be explicitly documented in the release notes or upgrade documentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/installation-and-upgrade/partials/snippet-check-rpmnew-rpmsave.adoc:2
msgid "Do not treat these files as a post-upgrade checklist or merge them in bulk. Only review a file if you are actively troubleshooting a specific issue and understand the impact of the configuration it contains. If a change is required, it should be applied intentionally based on a known requirement, not by copying differences from these files. If you are unsure, leave the file unchanged."
msgstr ""

